const articlePoints=["Use only the public description: assistance with purchases from Chinese online and offline channels, a pasted product link, and goods sent to a China warehouse. These facts do not prove stock, final price, delivery time or customs results.","A spreadsheet helps discovery but never replaces the live listing. Record the exact title, option, displayed price, seller and date; similar photographs can describe another version or size chart.","A pasted link is a product reference, not a promise that every option remains available. Note the selected variant and a clear reason to reject it; compare measurements, plugs, voltage and included accessories where relevant.","A displayed product price is not automatically the all-in cost. Product, domestic movement, service choices, international transport and destination charges can be separate, so use a budget that allows for change.","The stated China-warehouse stage separates seller dispatch from later delivery. Keep the listing, selected option and notes together; visible images can help comparison but cannot prove fit, material, durability, authenticity or future delivery.","Save the URL, name, option, price, currency, seller, date, measurements, photo notes and status. Flag unclear sizing, conflicting descriptions, promotional-only images and unusual prices instead of turning copied links into recommendations.","Ask checkable questions about material, measurement, selected option, accessory or current availability. Save the answer and date; an answer about one seller, parcel or destination is not a permanent rule for all others.","An independent guide cannot guarantee delivery dates, customs outcomes, duty amounts or authenticity. Those results depend on the parcel, destination, carrier, local rules and later events, so use check, compare, confirm and allow for change.","FindSpreadsheet supports further product research; it does not sell, verify or guarantee every item. Search concrete features, then use the current source listing for the final comparison.","Compare exact options, measurements, material wording, visible images, stated accessories and information shown by the seller, not only headline price. Mark missing facts; a lower price can mean a different version or missing accessory.","Listings, stock, options and quoted services can change. Date every finding and recheck important rows before submission. Label missing measurements, promotional photographs and later charges as uncertainty rather than certain facts.","Make small decisions: does the listing meet the need, is the option unambiguous, and what change makes you stop? Only then continue with the order flow; the warehouse is a later checkpoint, not a substitute for first research.","A listing supports claims about its displayed name, option, price or image; a public homepage supports the service it describes. Neither proves every seller, parcel, country or future result, so avoid guaranteed, cheapest or fastest language.","Set a maximum total and an exit condition before submitting a link. Keep the product cost, budget ceiling and unresolved questions together; if later information exceeds the rule, you can stop without rationalising the change.","The method is a calm sequence: verify the listing, record the selected option, separate facts from estimates and decide what evidence is needed next. It works for one item or a larger shortlist and makes later changes understandable.","Before submitting a link, reopen the listing, record the exact variant, remember the displayed price may not be the final cost, set an acceptance rule and recheck available evidence later. This independent guide does not process orders or payments."];
